import IUT.LeanForm
import IUT.Processes

/-!
# Stage 2 of the LeanForm of IUT: the proof of [IUTchIII] Thm 3.11 modulo [IUTchI-II]

[FormIUT] §2: *Stage 2: Proof of [IUTchIII] Theorem 3.11 modulo [IUTchI-II]*,
the stage that Stage 1 "just shows that what one is really interested in".
Theorem 3.11 constructs the **multiradial representation** of the Θ-pilot:

* (a) the tensor packets of log-shells `I_{S^±_{j+1}}`, `j = 0, …, l*`
  ([IUTchIII] Prop 3.1–3.3), built étale-theoretically from the vertically
  coric data of the 0-column of the log-theta-lattice (Thm 1.5, Prop 1.2);
* (b) the splitting monoids of the LGP-monoids, whose value-group portions
  are generated by `q̲_v^{j²}` (Prop 3.4–3.5, with the upper semi-compatibility
  (Ind3) of the log-Kummer correspondence);
* (c) the global realified Frobenioids `(F^⊛_mod)_j`, one copy for each
  `j ∈ F_l^*` (Prop 3.7, Ex 3.6);

and shows that the result is *multiradial*: it is defined on the étale-like
data of the codomain of the Θ-link up to the indeterminacies (Ind1), (Ind2),
(Ind3).  Its proof is a sequence of constructions of [IUTchIII] §1–§3 each of
which rests on results of [IUTchI-II]: the Hodge theaters and processions of
[IUTchI], and the Galois evaluation, conjugate synchronization, Kummer
isomorphisms and Θ×μ-links of [IUTchII].

This file is the skeletal Lean form of that proof on top of the data model of
this library:

* `inputs`: the results of [IUTchI-II] the proof uses, by process id;
  `steps`: the twelve constructions of [IUTchIII] §1–§3 (the twelve
  [IUTchIII] processes of `docs/PROCESSES.md` other than Cor 3.12), each
  with the part of Thm 3.11 it feeds and its inputs; `steps_acyclic`:
  every step depends only on earlier steps and on [IUTchI-II] inputs;
* `MultiradialData`, `ofEtHT`: the data (a)(b)(c) of Thm 3.11 constructed
  from an étale Hodge theater; `ofEtHT_packets_ind1`, `ofEtHT_shells_etale`,
  `ofEtHT_splitting`, `ofEtHT_global_length`, `ofEtHT_multiradial`: its
  properties; `ofEtHT_APT`: it depends only on the étale-like data;
  `toMltRep_eq_dsc`: it is what the descent arrow of Stage 1 computes;
* `logLink_shares_etHT_G`, `thetaLink_shares_etHT_G`: the étale data the
  construction uses is vertically coric ((Stp2) of [FormIUT] §3) and its
  mono-analytic part is horizontally coric ((Stp3));
* `LogVolumeSpace`, `ThmThreeEleven`, `thmThreeElevenFive_of_thmThreeEleven`,
  `corThreeTwelve_of_thmThreeEleven`: the **common-container comparison** of
  Stage 1 — the single hypothesis left open there — is *derived* from the
  statement of Thm 3.11 together with Def 3.8 (ii) (the Θ-link sends the
  Θ-pilot to the q-pilot) and Prop 3.9–3.10 (the log-volumes and their
  monotonicity).  Those are now the explicit hypotheses, each a result of
  [IUTchIII] whose proof is the subject of this stage, modulo [IUTchI-II].
-/

namespace IUT

namespace StageTwo

/-! ## The inputs from [IUTchI-II] -/

/-- A result of [IUTchI-II] used by the proof of Thm 3.11, by the id of the
process of `docs/PROCESSES.md` that implements it. -/
structure Input where
  id : String
  paper : Paper
  ref : String
  statement : String
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- The inputs from [IUTchI-II]. -/
def inputs : List Input := [
  ⟨"BuildProcessions", .IUTchI, "[IUTchI] Prop 4.11, Prop 6.9",
    "the processions S^±_{j+1} = {0, …, j} that index the tensor packets"⟩,
  ⟨"GlueHodgeTheaters", .IUTchI, "[IUTchI] Prop 6.7, Def 6.13",
    "the Θ±ell NF-Hodge theaters, the vertices of the lattice"⟩,
  ⟨"ForgetToDHodgeTheater", .IUTchI, "[IUTchI] Def 6.13, Rem 6.12.2",
    "the étale-like D-Θ±ell NF-Hodge theater (etHT)"⟩,
  ⟨"BuildGlobalRealified", .IUTchI, "[IUTchI] Ex 3.5",
    "the global realified Frobenioids F⊩_mod with the gluing data ρ_v"⟩,
  ⟨"AssembleThetaHodgeTheater", .IUTchI, "[IUTchI] Def 3.6, Cor 3.7",
    "the Θ-link as a full poly-isomorphism of F⊩-strips preserving D⊢_v and O×"⟩,
  ⟨"EvaluateTheta", .IUTchII, "[IUTchII] Cor 2.4, 2.5, 2.8",
    "Galois evaluation of the theta function at the l-torsion points: Θ ↦ q̲^{j²}"⟩,
  ⟨"BuildMonoids", .IUTchII, "[IUTchII] Prop 3.1, Cor 3.5-3.7, 4.5-4.6",
